    {
      "title": "Albanese government warned it’s ‘sleepwalking into another robodebt scenario’ over use of algorithms and AI",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/05/albanese-government-warned-its-sleepwalking-into-another-robodebt-scenario-over-use-of-algorithms-and-ai",
      "description": "<p>Centre for Public Integrity report says mandatory audit and public register of all automated decision-making needed</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The federal government is “sleepwalking its way into another robodebt” scandal amid a lack of transparency and legislation around use of algorithms and artificial intelligence in decisions, the chief executive of independent thinktank the Centre for Public Integrity said.</p><p>Dr Catherine Williams launched the centre’s “Computer Says No” report on Thursday, which examines the use of automated decision-making (ADM) tools by the government and calls for urgent reform.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/05/albanese-government-warned-its-sleepwalking-into-another-robodebt-scenario-over-use-of-algorithms-and-ai\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T14:00:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "Australia has an especially bad inflation problem. So why are we only middle-of-the pack on the misery index?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/05/australian-economy-inflation-cost-of-living-misery-index",
      "description": "<p>Comparing Australia to other countries may not be much comfort but does offer some perspective on the economy</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Is Australia’s inflation problem worse than the rest of the world’s?</p><p>A day after the Reserve Bank delivered its <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/03/rba-interest-rates-decision-cash-rate-november-reserve-bank-australia\">fifth interest rate hike</a> for the year, increasingly stressed mortgage holders would be justified asking.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/nov/05/australian-economy-inflation-cost-of-living-misery-index\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T14:00:37"
    },
    {
      "title": "‘Discontent and distrust’: annual social cohesion checkup shows exactly what’s making Australia angry",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/04/social-cohesion-report-australia-cost-of-living-economy-immigration-multiculturalism-ai-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Cost of living and AI outrank climate change and war as top concerns for future, but support for multiculturalism remains strong</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The vast majority of Australians support immigration and multiculturalism despite more feeling poorer – and increasingly pessimistic and distrustful of government, the annual Scanlon report on social cohesion has revealed.</p><p>People are more worried about artificial intelligence than climate change or going to war, but a global economic downturn and cost-of-living pressures are Australians’ key concerns.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/04/social-cohesion-report-australia-cost-of-living-economy-immigration-multiculturalism-ai-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-11-04T14:00:36"
    },
    {
      "title": "Muslim Votes Matter softens anti-Labor stance ahead of Victorian election in bid to defeat One Nation in at-risk seats",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/05/muslim-votes-matter-softens-anti-labor-stance-victoria-election-one-nation-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p><strong>Exclusive:</strong> Advocacy group will put volunteers on the ground in Labor-held outer suburban seats that could swing towards Pauline Hanson’s party</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily political email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Muslim Votes Matter will relax its anti-Labor position at this month’s Victorian election, putting volunteers on the ground in key outer suburban seats the incumbent government risks losing to One Nation.</p><p>The grassroots advocacy group will direct its supporters to vote for Labor ahead of Pauline Hanson’s party in all lower house Victorian electorates and will aim to have volunteers on the ground in the seats of Greenvale, in Melbourne’s north, and Narre Warren South, in the city’s south-east, which the party fears could be seized by One Nation.</p><p><strong><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/28/politics-really-newsletter-guardian-australia-free-best-daily-auspol-email-subscribe?CMP=copyembed\">Sign up for Guardian Australia’s Politics, really newsletter here</a></strong></p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/nov/05/muslim-votes-matter-softens-anti-labor-stance-victoria-election-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
